INSERT INTO feature VALUES('glf-face-theory','descriptions','GLF: the finite shape theory','glf-two-views','implemented','uncommon','dependent provers','Finite shapes as a FaceTT shape parameter with no interval: decidable subshapes with complements, meets, unions and the outer pushout (UnionSquare::mediator); atomic and conjunctive entailment (decide) with a Derivation or a Countermodel, each validated independently of the search; a conclusion''s column disjunctions admitted, as membership in a union; a query whose every atom is monotone (the whole carrier, the empty subshape, or the upper point of a carrier of two points) admitted with free connectives and decided in the normal forms of the free distributive lattice, its evidence a cover of each premise term and a normal form past 1024 terms refused; any other disjunction across variables or in a premise refused at admission; evidence by meets and covers, not case trees. A theory block names the shape''s points by `boundary` and its faces by `face`, read through the nominal Boundary into Fin(m) in name order. A record type''s labels are a boundary too, and its `where` block names faces over them, a face listing a label the record lacks refused at the label.','theory-shapes surface-lowering','crates/theory-shapes/tests/finite.rs crates/theory-shapes/tests/faces.rs crates/theory-shapes/tests/cubes.rs corpus/model/desc/record-faces.gandr corpus/pathological/desc/record-faces.gandr','crate-tests','#640');
